# 🟢 8️⃣ $project (Reshaping Data)

Suppose we want:

Only:

* userId
* amount
* hide _id

```js
db.transactions.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      userId: 1,
      amount: 1
    }
  }
])
```

Used in:

* API responses
* Data transformation
* Hiding internal fields

---

# 🟢 9️⃣ Real Production Example — Fraud Detection

Fraud team wants:

👉 Users who made more than 10 transactions in 1 minute.

Pipeline logic:

* Group by userId
* Count transactions
* Filter count > 10

```js
db.transactions.aggregate([
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$userId",
      count: { $sum: 1 }
    }
  },
  {
    $match: { count: { $gt: 10 } }
  }
])
```

Used in:

* Real-time monitoring
* Anti-money laundering

